{"author":"Joe Oakhart","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"7d2888eb5ed3dce9455e1a5c5de750e08ee013018d281166d10d57e34ecdfa1c","digest":{"component_or_area":"fetcher._iter_pages pagination","key_entities":["src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/fetcher.py","fetcher._iter_pages","fetcher.collect","_build_snapshot","jira.search.views.default.max","start_at","page_size","SilentTruncationError","get_parent_map","change 1105","change 1118"],"problem_keywords":["pagination","truncation","data loss","inbound snapshot","page termination","offset pagination"],"propositions":["_iter_pages terminates on a short page and advances by requested page_size, causing server-truncated pages to be mistaken for end-of-results","92% of issues are silently lost from the inbound snapshot when a Jira Data Center server caps pages below the requested size","the defect affects the shared core fetcher path used by both Cloud and DC adapters, not just the DC adapter","the fix must advance by len(page) and terminate only on empty pages, matching the prior correction to get_parent_map","an offset-stall guard is needed to raise SilentTruncationError instead of looping when a server ignores startAt and returns the same non-empty page indefinitely"]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787540574916948001,"uuid":"b8f434f3-964e-4a64-85e5-d5908bf6a1b1"}